 SUMMARY: 3.1 Summary: The xfmrnowst1-nowst1_rev23 constraint (NOWST1 345/138kV transformer) bound in the Day-Ahead market on August 13, 2026, driven by extreme summer peak load in the OKGE zone and a massive over-forecast of wind generation. OKGE load is the dominant structural driver of this constraint, pulling power through the transformer. On the target date, SPP system load reached the 99.7th percentile. The DA/RT divergence (DA bound at -1989, RT cleared at 0) was caused by a 5,626 MW over-forecast of wind at the binding hour (HE 17). Since wind in OKGE is a loading driver, the DA model placed significantly more flow on the constraint than materialized in RT, causing it to bind only in DA. 
